################################################################################################
# ADMISSIBILITY OF EACH CONVENTION, MEASURED (a rule under which the metric is the
# same number on all three machines AND pooled is CONSTANT-BY-ALGEBRA, not a rival
# reading of the data).  Classified by measurement, never by a hand-kept exemption
# list: an exemption list goes stale silently, this cannot.
################################################################################################
  M1   admissible U-rules: ['U-DROP']   [U-SELF=CONSTANT-BY-ALGEBRA(1.0000); U-SPLIT=CONSTANT-BY-ALGEBRA(1.0000)]
  M2   admissible U-rules: ['U-DROP', 'U-SELF']   [U-SPLIT=ALIAS of U-DROP]
  M3   admissible U-rules: ['U-DROP']   [U-SELF=ALIAS of U-DROP; U-SPLIT=ALIAS of U-DROP]
  NC   admissible U-rules: ['U-DROP']   [U-SELF=ALIAS of U-DROP; U-SPLIT=ALIAS of U-DROP]
  M1   admissible specs:   ['S0-PRIMARY', 'S1-OWN-ONLY', 'S2-TOKENS-ONLY']   [S3-NO-MAC=ALIAS of S0-PRIMARY]
  M2   admissible specs:   ['S0-PRIMARY', 'S1-OWN-ONLY', 'S2-TOKENS-ONLY', 'S3-NO-MAC']
  M3   admissible specs:   ['S0-PRIMARY']   [S1-OWN-ONLY=ALIAS of S0-PRIMARY; S2-TOKENS-ONLY=ALIAS of S0-PRIMARY; S3-NO-MAC=ALIAS of S0-PRIMARY]
  NC   admissible specs:   ['S0-PRIMARY', 'S1-OWN-ONLY', 'S2-TOKENS-ONLY', 'S3-NO-MAC']

################################################################################################
# LEVEL swings (DIAGNOSTIC, NOT THE GATE) and the firing world of each gate version
################################################################################################
  metric   gen-0 (S0,U-DROP)  level swing, U  level swing, spec       MDE   admissible d.o.f.
  M1                  0.4567          0.5433             0.2561    0.2600   U:1
          ORIGINAL GATE VACUOUS BOTH WAYS: counting the inadmissible rules it fires for every detectable effect; striking them it can never fire.
  M2                  0.2348          0.1276             0.3072    0.3036   U:2
          original gate well defined (>=2 admissible U-rules, non-zero swing)
          ⚠ PRE-DATA WARNING (diagnostic, NOT a gate verdict): the gen-0 LEVEL swing across admissible specifications is 0.3072 >= MDE 0.3036.
          A level swing is not an effect; the amended gate compares effect-to-effect and can only be evaluated at E.  But a metric whose LEVEL moves by more than its own MDE under a defensible re-reading is fragile, and this is said before the data, not after.
  M3                 46.6054          0.0000             0.0000   34.9470   U:1
          ORIGINAL GATE VACUOUS: every U-rule is an ALIAS here, so its zero swing measures no robustness at all.
  NC                  0.3842          0.0000             0.2366    0.2310   U:1
          ORIGINAL GATE VACUOUS: every U-rule is an ALIAS here, so its zero swing measures no robustness at all.
          ⚠ PRE-DATA WARNING (diagnostic, NOT a gate verdict): the gen-0 LEVEL swing across admissible specifications is 0.2366 >= MDE 0.2310.
          A level swing is not an effect; the amended gate compares effect-to-effect and can only be evaluated at E.  But a metric whose LEVEL moves by more than its own MDE under a defensible re-reading is fragile, and this is said before the data, not after.

